  "details": "A constant pain point for OSC app developers is that VRChat writes out the osc config once, and then never updates it when avatar parameters have changed, requiring the user to either manually reset the config or delete the OSC folder (very poor experience).\n\nThe number of users that modify these configs is likely to be extremely low, compared to the users who simply want OSC to output all avatar parameters all the time.\n\nI propose a simple solution:\n\nVRChat should write the example config to `OSC/avtr_*.json.example`, but only ever read it from the existing location, `OSC/avtr_*.json`.\n\nThis way, users who do not remove the .example file extension will always use a default fresh \"all parameters\" config.",
